use std
into drive_icon.amni
lang amni
Native Helium and Gold adaptive app icon renderer for Amni-Drive. Generates crisp anti-aliased RGBA renders of the Amni-Drive obsidian-midnight chrono dial and sculpted ivory-gold chevron emblem across full-bleed adaptive, rounded-squircle, and circular masks.
Struct `Img` holds `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers and `px` as a growable byte buffer of length `w` times `h` times 4 in RGBA order.
Function `clampf` takes `v`, `lo`, and `hi` as 32-bit floats and returns `v` clamped between `lo` and `hi`.
Function `lerpf` takes `a`, `b`, and `t` as 32-bit floats and returns linear interpolation between `a` and `b` at `t` clamped to 0.0 through 1.0.
Function `mix_rgb` takes `a` and `b` as unsigned 32-bit ARGB colors and `t` as a 32-bit float, returning linearly interpolated ARGB color with alpha 255.
Function `blend` takes a mutable `Img` `im`, `x` and `y` as 32-bit integers, `col` as an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color, and `cov` as a 32-bit float coverage, alpha-blending source color onto destination pixel in `im.px` when coordinates are in bounds and effective alpha is positive.
Function `point_in_tri` takes `px`, `py`, `ax`, `ay`, `bx`, `by`, `cx`, `cy` as 32-bit floats and returns true when point `(px, py)` lies inside or on the triangle `(ax, ay)`, `(bx, by)`, `(cx, cy)`.
Function `dist_seg` takes `px`, `py`, `ax`, `ay`, `bx`, `by` as 32-bit floats and returns Euclidean distance from `(px, py)` to segment `(ax, ay)` through `(bx, by)`.
Function `sdf_tri` takes `px`, `py`, `ax`, `ay`, `bx`, `by`, `cx`, `cy` as 32-bit floats and returns signed distance (negative inside, positive outside) to the triangle using `point_in_tri` and minimum `dist_seg` across all 3 edges.
Function `sdf_squircle` takes `nx`, `ny`, `half`, and `rad` as 32-bit floats and returns signed distance to a rounded square centered at the origin with half-size `half` and corner radius `rad`.
Function `render_drive_icon` takes `size` as a 32-bit integer and `mask_mode` as a 32-bit integer (0 for full square, 1 for rounded-squircle launcher icon, 2 for circular round launcher icon) and returns an `Img` of size `size` by `size` rendered with 2x2 supersampling per pixel in normalized 108-unit Android adaptive coordinates (`0.0` to `108.0`, center `54.0, 54.0`):
- Step 1: Background obsidian-midnight cockpit gradient sweeping diagonally from `#060A14` at top-left to `#0F1F36` at bottom-right, layered with an upper-left cool sapphire specular glow (`#3878C8FF` centered at `28, 22`, radius `64`) and a subtle lower-right warm amber rim sheen (`#24F5B041` centered at `86, 88`, radius `54`).
- Step 2: Recessed dark chrono dial cavity centered at `(54, 54)` with radius `31.0`, soft drop shadow shifted downward by `2.4` units, cavity fill radial gradient from `#0D1729` center to `#050912` edge, and thin subtle metallic inner track ring at radius `29.2` (`#FF223650`, half-width `0.85`).
- Step 3: Precision 240-degree brushed gold outer cockpit bezel arc centered at `(54, 54)` with radius `26.8` and stroke half-width `2.8` sweeping clockwise over the top from angle `-122` degrees to `+122` degrees relative to 12 o'clock (where 0 degrees is straight up `(0, -1)` and positive angles rotate clockwise), with smooth rounded arc endcaps and metallic gold gradient (`#FFFFE5A3` top highlight transitioning smoothly to `#FFC9892C` at the lower ends).
- Step 4: Illuminated electric cyan-to-mint active velocity arc layered cleanly over the upper-right sweep of the dial track at radius `26.8` (half-width `2.6`) from `+8` degrees to `+102` degrees clockwise with rounded endcaps, subtle cyan outer glow halo (`radius 26.8`, half-width `6.2`, alpha `0.30`, `#FF22D3EE`), and crisp gradient fill from `#FF22D3EE` to `#FF24F5B2`.
- Step 5: 13 precision radial gauge tick marks along the inner dial rim (`radius 20.5` to `23.0`) spaced evenly every `20` degrees from `-120` to `+120` degrees; major cardinal ticks (`-120`, `-60`, `0`, `+60`, `+120`) are bright ivory-gold (`#FFE8C882`, width `1.3`) and minor ticks are crisp muted slate (`#FF6B85A6`, width `0.85`).
- Step 6: Sculpted Amni-Drive faceted forward chevron emblem centered inside the dial (`tip` at `(54, 32.5)`, `left wing` at `(37.5, 68.0)`, `right wing` at `(70.5, 68.0)`, `center notch` at `(54, 59.5)`):
  - Soft dark drop shadow offset `(0, 2.2)` beneath both wings for crisp floating depth.
  - Left facet triangle `(54, 32.5)-(37.5, 68.0)-(54, 59.5)` filled with bright ivory-white gradient (`#FFFFFFFF` top to `#FFEAE4D6` bottom) with rounded vertex sheen.
  - Right facet triangle `(54, 32.5)-(54, 59.5)-(70.5, 68.0)` filled with brushed champagne Amni-Gold gradient (`#FFF6D38B` top to `#FFC88B2E` bottom).
- Step 7: Subtle brushed lower cockpit horizon arc beneath the chevron (`radius 26.8`, from `+142` to `+218` degrees at bottom center, thin `1.2` stroke in `#FF2C425E`) completing the automotive instrument silhouette cleanly.
- Step 8: Apply `mask_mode` anti-aliased alpha mask: when `mask_mode` equals 1 apply `sdf_squircle` (half `49.5`, corner radius `22.5` in 108-unit space); when `mask_mode` equals 2 apply circle mask (`radius 50.0` centered at `54, 54`); when `mask_mode` equals 3 omit the background gradient (transparent adaptive foreground layer); when `mask_mode` equals 0 leave full square opaque.
Function `write_ppm_rgba` writes binary PAM (`P7`) RGBA file with transparency to `path` (width, height, depth 4, maxval 255, tupltype RGB_ALPHA) so Python or ImageMagick can convert directly to lossless transparent PNGs across all mipmap densities.
Function `main` renders `512x512` squircle showcase to `"/tmp/amni_drive_icon/icon_512_squircle.pam"`, `512x512` circle preview to `"/tmp/amni_drive_icon/icon_512_round.pam"`, `512x512` full-bleed adaptive preview to `"/tmp/amni_drive_icon/icon_512_full.pam"`, and `432x432` transparent adaptive foreground to `"/tmp/amni_drive_icon/icon_432_fg.pam"`, then prints `"rendered amni-drive gold+helium icons ok"`.
